      "properties": {
        "reported": true,
        "property_type": "optical",
        "summary": "Solid-state fluorescence at room temperature shows characteristic Eu(III) emission under 260 nm excitation at 540, 592, 617 and 700 nm. UV–Vis spectra of 1–3 in methanol are similar, with a ligand-related band near 247 nm and a red-shifted absorption around 319 nm versus free H2L. Lifetime and quantum-yield values for 1 are mentioned but not numerically readable in the converted text.",
